 "overview": "The Medford Energy and Environment Committee is an advisory and municipal working group focused on building decarbonization, renewable energy, waste reduction, tree canopy preservation, and environmental stewardship in Medford. The archive documents 30 meetings of the committee held between November 2022 and October 2026. Over this span, the body has coordinated citywide educational events, reviewed state and local climate policy, endorsed tree preservation ordinances, and supported community heat pump adoption. At its most recent meetings, the committee continued monitoring progress on the city's Climate Action and Adaptation Plan, prepared for the annual Harvest Your Energy Festival, and explored policy options to restrict anticoagulant rodenticides.",
