   "name": "Tree protection and tree ordinances",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee has dedicated sustained work to expanding Medford's tree canopy and establishing municipal tree protections. Early efforts evaluated canopy data using iTree software and reviewed draft ordinances dividing regulations between public land, private land, and a municipal tree committee [M04#2, M05#6, M07#10]. In January 2024, the committee voted to endorse the tree ordinance drafts submitted to the City Council [M13#4]. The body subsequently tracked council discussions regarding enforcement capacity, canopy goals, and mitigation fees [M15#3, M21#5]. In mid-2026, members noted a favorable vote by the City Council Committee of the Whole on the public tree ordinance while continuing to monitor state tree protection legislation and local planting programs [M28#4, M29#3, M29#8].",
