   "summary": "Efforts to decarbonize residential and municipal buildings began with presentations on heat pump technology, financing programs, and volunteer coaching models used in neighboring communities [M01#2, M03#8, M08#6]. The committee reviewed proposals for an outreach grant that established the Electrify Medford campaign, aiming to provide resident consultations and address cold-weather concerns [M09#5, M13#6]. City staff routinely delivered updates on coach training, Mass Save partnership enrollment, and outreach at civic festivals [M14#3, M17#2, M22#5]. Decarbonization discussions subsequently broadened to encompass municipal building roadmaps, geothermal feasibility, and school HVAC replacements through 2026 [M18#3, M21#4, M27#4].",
