   "name": "Waste management and zero-waste initiatives",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee regularly monitors municipal waste contracts and develops zero-waste initiatives. Early discussions covered procurement for multi-year waste contracts, event composting feasibility, and the rollout of citywide curbside composting [M03#3, M09#4, M14#3, M17#4]. The body later formed an informal zero-waste working group and developed a business survey regarding the transition away from single-use black plastic takeout containers [M21#3, M24#3, M25#7, M29#1]. In 2026, the committee engaged in extended debates over a municipal proposal to transition to bi-weekly trash collection and implement a pay-as-you-throw framework, balancing diversion benefits against rodent control and household concerns [M26#2, M27#7].",
