   "name": "Rodent control and rodenticide restrictions",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Prompted by poisonings of local wildlife, the committee began investigating alternatives to anticoagulant rodenticides and advocating for non-toxic pest management [M06#6, M07#6]. Discussions covered integrated pest management strategies, rodent birth control, and coordinating public education alongside municipal health officials [M06#6, M08#4]. Members monitored state legislative bills restricting toxic rodenticides and reviewed local authority to regulate their deployment [M20#8, M21#7, M27#6]. By late 2026, the committee continued researching municipal restriction policies and hosted Save Arlington Wildlife to evaluate ecological damage and alternative abatement measures [M29#6, M30#7].",
