   "name": "Climate Action Plan and resilience tracking",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee tracks citywide climate vulnerability, greenhouse gas metrics, and implementation of Medford's Climate Action Plan. Initial meetings focused on regional watershed flood mitigation, Amelia Earhart Dam protection, and stormwater infrastructure grants [M09#6, M10#2, M18#4]. In late 2025, the committee received the city's greenhouse gas emissions inventory and established a process to track specific action items in the Climate Action Plan [M25#4, M25#6]. This tracking continued across subsequent sessions, reviewing items including zoning recodification, municipal energy reductions, and gap analyses leading into the plan's five-year review [M27#5, M29#9, M30#6].",
